<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Choice dives into loss, seeks more capital.</title>
<headline>Choice dives into loss, seeks more capital.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Feb 28, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr loss (cts)	  338.2	 vs  91.8 profit</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   nil</p>
<p>    Attrib loss		45.70	vs  10.92 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss	     89.68	vs   6.82 profit</p>
<p>    Tax credit		  1.28	vs   4.82 charge</p>
<p>    Finance costs	    38.73	vs  14.89</p>
<p>    Turnover		  572.40	vs 432.20</p>
<p>Full name: Choice Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The poultry and meat company had warned shareholders last month that the total attributable loss for the year ended February 28, 1997 would be greater than anticipated.</p>
<p>The company had a 102 million rand rights issue in December 1996 but said that in view of the continued losses further sources of fixed capital were now being sought. Yabeng Investment Holding Co Ltd, which has a stake in the firm, had provided a further 40 million rand since the year-end, it added.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
